WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.130
SPEAKER 1: You may spend a
lot of your time writing code.

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:04.450
I certainly do.

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:09.100
With every keystroke, you and I
are creating future liability.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.010
The code we write has to be
tested, deployed, debugged,

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.800
maintained, stored,
and, one day, retired.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.580
That's expensive.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.020
What we really want is
to process business data.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.600
Code is just a way to get
there, but there are other ways.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.800
Here's how I reduce the amount
of code I have to write.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.830
One, I use Cloud Run to
go serverless instead

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:32.270
of mucking about with servers.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:34.180
Two, I use Google
Cloud Workflows

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.700
to orchestrate my
services with simple YAML,

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.350
instead of with code.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:42.640
Three, I let my users enter
and view data in Google Sheets,

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.160
instead of building
custom interfaces.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:48.760
Four, I use Google Data
Studio to create dashboards,

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.650
instead of building
them with code.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.920
Five, I use AppSheet to
create data-centric apps

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.600
with zero code.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.000
What's your favorite
way to reduce code?

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.330
Let me know in the comments.

